\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.4}{\ignorespaces TMA benchmark: (a) On-axis PSFs at $\lambda = 0.65\,\mu \mathrm  {m}$: the observed misaligned PSF (Gaussian noise, $\sigma = 0.01\%$ of the ideal peak), the Nautilus starting point (median of the final 100 posterior samples), during differential evolution (DE) at generations 40, 114, 218 and 402 (A--D), and after 2000 generations (final). Intensity is relative to the aligned system's peak, so each panel's peak equals its Strehl ratio (log stretch, floor $10^{-4}$). Values are RMS wavefront error in waves, the RMS of the OPD difference from the nominal design. (b) RMS WFE of the best DE member at each generation; letters mark the PSFs in (a). (c) Best-member value of each alignment parameter at each generation (blue) and the injected truth (gray).\relax }}{42}{figure.caption.26}\protected@file@percent }
